# No nested wait on the UI thread

Do not block the UI thread on FFmpeg or ffprobe. That includes `QProcess::waitForFinished`, `QEventLoop::exec()`, and a `processEvents` loop until a terminal flag.

Keep the `QProcess` signal-driven (`finished` / `errorOccurred`). A window-modal `QProgressDialog` stays open until that signal; the caller continues in a queued callback or `runFinished`. `setAutoClose(false)` and `setAutoReset(false)`. Close the dialog with `QSignalBlocker` so `canceled` cannot re-enter.

A short probe that already has a synchronous parser may run on a worker via `QtConcurrent::run`. Continue on the UI thread with `QFutureWatcher`. Do not `QFuture::waitForFinished()` on the UI thread.

```cpp
// BAD — nested loop re-enters start/cancel and freezes the window
while (!finished_) {
  QCoreApplication::processEvents(QEventLoop::AllEvents, 100);
}

// GOOD — dialog is window-modal; the real event loop keeps running
progress->setAutoClose(false);
progress->setAutoReset(false);
connect(process, &QProcess::finished, this, &Preparer::onProcessFinished);
progress->show();
```
